Z||000000||84_duke||10-24-2001||07:56 PM||||I was just looking at the Ocelot Performance Exhaust from the Fiero Store.<BR>Does anyone know how much of a performance increase I could expect from installing this in my 84 indy?  Is it worth it for triple the price of installing the stock exhaust?<BR>Thanks in advance!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-24-2001||09:18 PM||||I doubt that you would notice any remarkable improvement with a new exhaust on an 84 2.5 L engine that the pace car had.  Lets say you get 10% increase 92+9= 101HP.  Still not a tire burning 160 mph Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dave Gunsul||10-24-2001||11:52 PM||||I've got the Ocelot system on my GT and it really didn't make that much of a difference.<BR>Unlike the original exhaust it can rust too.<BR>The Borla system is the best exhaust for the Fiero when performance is concerned but it<BR>is very expensive.<BR>Your best be would probably be to put a high<BR>flow cat on, or remove completely, and then<BR>buy a performance muffler that you can put in place of the original.<BR>Some people put a muffler where the cat was <BR>and just run a straight pipe where the<BR>muffler was.<BR>When you're going for more power every little bit helps though so any improvement will be just that, an improvement.<P>BTW Holley still make a header for the 84-86<BR>4 cyl.'s.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
